  "body": "## What changed\n\n- The default depth ladder does not change. It keeps the remainder in the last step. `top 20, bottom 2, stepdown 5` cuts `[15, 10, 5, 2]`.\n- A new operation parameter, `equal_steps`, is in the `links.approach` object. The default is off.\n- With `equal_steps` on, the ladder cuts the same number of levels in equal steps. The same example cuts `[15.5, 11, 6.5, 2]`.\n- `camcraft_motion::machining2d::equal_stepdown` gives the stepdown of the equal ladder. The level law `cut_levels_under` walks it. There is still one level law.\n- `cut_levels_for(top, &approach, bottom, stepdown)` reads the mode and the stock top from the approach. These ladders call it: 2D Pocket (rings, adaptive, HSM, trochoidal, avoid), 2D Adaptive rest, 2D Contour, Slot, Bore, Circular (and its vault rings), 3D Pocket (plain, shell, rest refine).\n- With stock above Top Z (#2004), the level at Top Z stays. The steps below it are equal.\n- The project file writes `equal_steps` only when it is on. Older files load without a change.\n- The params digest takes one byte only when the mode is on. The stamp of each existing operation does not change.\n- The pocket region law of the app (`operation::area::ladder_planes`) reads the same mode through `OpParams::ladder_stepdown`. The region is built at the planes that the generator cuts.\n- The Lead in / Lead out tab has one new row, \"Equal depth steps\", in the Linking group.\n- `docs/decisions/2012-equal-steps.md` records the decision.\n\nThe parameter is undoable through `EditOperationParams`. The MCP `edit_operation` patch reaches it as `params.links.approach.equal_steps`. No new command and no new MCP tool are necessary.\n\n## Cause\n\nIssue #2012 asks for a decision between a remainder last step and equal steps. The level law had only the remainder ladder. The project rule \"CAM choices are parameters\" asks for a parameter with a default.\n\n## Scope limit\n\nFace, Trace, Engrave and Trochoidal Slot have no `links` object. They cannot save the parameter and keep the remainder ladder. Issue #2832 adds the parameter to them. Turning has its own infeed laws and is not part of this change.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins in `crates/motion/tests/equal_steps.rs`:\n\n- `the_default_ladder_keeps_the_remainder_and_equal_steps_is_opt_in`\n- `equal_steps_keep_the_level_count_and_never_pass_the_stepdown`\n- `equal_steps_keep_the_level_at_top_z_under_stock`\n- `equal_steps_refuse_what_the_remainder_ladder_refuses`\n- `a_pocket_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_trochoidal_adaptive_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_contour_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_slot_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_bore_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_circular_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `a_3d_pocket_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n\nPins in `crates/app/tests/equal_steps.rs`:\n\n- `edit_sets_equal_steps_and_undo_restores_the_remainder_ladder`\n- `the_project_file_writes_equal_steps_only_when_on_and_reads_it_back`\n- `the_stamp_tells_the_two_ladders_apart`\n- `the_region_law_reads_the_stepdown_of_the_ladder_mode`\n- `the_generated_contour_cuts_the_levels_of_its_mode`\n- `mcp_edit_operation_reaches_equal_steps`\n\nRed before the change: yes. The motion pin did not compile on `upstream/main` 3970d3d03 (`Approach` has no field `equal_steps`; `cut_levels_for` and `equal_stepdown` do not exist).\n\nMutation results:\n\n- Mutation 1: `ladder_stepdown` ignores the mode. Result: red. 10 of the 11 motion pins fail. The refusal pin stays green, which is correct.\n- Mutation 2: the 12 caller files are the files of `upstream/main`, and the new law stays. Result: red. The 7 operation pins fail. The 4 law pins stay green.\n- Mutation 3: the digest byte and the DTO write are removed. Result: red. `the_stamp_tells_the_two_ladders_apart`, `the_project_file_writes_equal_steps_only_when_on_and_reads_it_back` and `mcp_edit_operation_reaches_equal_steps` fail.\n- After each mutation the code was restored and the pins were green again.\n\nThe first stamp pin did not fail in mutation 3. A default approach hashes no bytes, so each approach that is not the default already has a different stamp. The pin now also compares two approaches that are not the default.\n\nGate:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` ran on `6ba261db2`: 162 steps, 161 green, 1 red.\n- The red step was `ui suites: lib`. The test binary stopped with `signal: 11, SIGSEGV` after 3 s. No test reported a failure.\n- The same step ran again alone (`--failed`) with no code change. It was green in 205 s.\n- An intermittent SIGSEGV of a UI test binary on `main` is recorded in #2807. Its cause is not known. This run does not show whether this PR is related to it.\n- After the gate, one assert line in `crates/motion/tests/equal_steps.rs` changed for clippy (head `13c4dffab`). The motion pins ran again and are green. The full quick gate did not run again on that head.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean on the final head.\n\nFile length: `crates/motion/src/approach.rs` was 440 lines and is now 446. `crates/motion/src/machining3d/entry.rs` is now 402 lines.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. `git diff --stat upstream/main...HEAD -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"*.cnc\"` is empty. The default ladder is the same.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No pin generates these ladders with the mode on: the pocket with keep-out areas (`pocket_avoid`), the 2D Adaptive rest ladder, the Circular vault rings, the 3D Pocket shell and rest-refine ladders, the rotary and multi-axis roughing. They call the same function as the pinned ladders.\n- No pin generates a pocket on a part with the mode on. `the_region_law_reads_the_stepdown_of_the_ladder_mode` pins the stepdown that the region law reads, not the region.\n- Code that reads `stepdown` as a bound is not changed (the 3-D shell floor below a plane, the first entry height of the contour). With equal steps it reads a bound a little larger than the real step. The decision file records this.\n- The new UI row has no test of its own. No snapshot PNG is changed.\n- The heavy lanes (`cargo xtask gate heavy`) were not run.\n- Nothing was run on a machine or in the stock simulation.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #2678 (`needs-rework`, `conflicts`) changes `crates/motion/src/machining3d/entry.rs`. It replaces the same `cut_levels_under` calls with its own `floor_levels::cut_levels`. It also changes `levels.rs`, but in `run_level_walks`, which this PR does not change. This PR is not stacked on #2678, because #2678 does not merge with `main` now. Whichever merges second refreshes, and must keep the mode in the 3-D ladder.\n- #2796 changes `crates/app/src/operation/area.rs`, in a different function. Whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #2716 and #2714 change `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`. This PR does not change that file.\n\nBuild note: the shared sccache server on the build machine did not answer. The tests and gates ran with `RUSTC_WRAPPER=` and `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: Depth ladder: new operation parameter \"Equal depth steps\" (off by default) cuts the same number of levels in equal steps; the default ladder keeps the remainder in the last step (#2012).\n\nFixes #2012\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
